{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/952975-whats-the-most-morally-ethically-fucked-up-things-your-pc-s-ever-done","id":952975,"title":"Whats the most Morally/Ethically fucked up things your PC's ever done","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-17T21:38:41-07:00","id":952975,"title":"Whats the most Morally/Ethically fucked up things your PC's ever done","content":"so...whats the darkest thing they have done?<br /> <br /> also, sorry to the moderators if this topic goes incredibly bitter, sour or just plain wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:03:55-07:00","id":953031,"title":"","content":"Well not done right now but it will come up next session. I used a the good old story arc of a primogen hates a neonate for some legitimate reason, while the neonate had also a good reason to kill the last descendant of the primogens mortal family. Long story short I originally intended that the players help one of to get ride of the problem. But the PC with humanity rating of 4 suggested that she kills one of her mortal family instead. This was so hilariously evil I up the ante, now the PC have to convince the neonate to kill a mortal family members who could procreate or forging evidence to call a blood hunt on the young neonate. <br /> Nobody wanted to go against the elder. Fun stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:38:05-07:00","id":953041,"title":"","content":"I was playing a Tzimisce in a Sabbat game. The pack wanted to take over a farmstead outside the city as a HQ for scouting the Camerilla city we was at. I decided to toy with the family before we claimed the farm. As the parents slept I crept into the baby's room, used Visiccitude to take the baby's face. I then stretched it over the tube of the TV and turned it on with the snow playing behind the face's eyes and mouth. Waited for the parents to wake, then tied their small intestines together around the bed post so they couldn't leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:13:07-07:00","id":953106,"title":"","content":"Yes, Sabbat games get dark quick. I never particularly have that problem because my players always know a) there is karma in my games and b) I reward heroic behavior. That being said, I have had players that have tried going beyond the pale. I will describe the worst incident in only three words: razors, battery acid, and chains. There is nothing that you can imagine that will be as cruel or as dark as that gaming session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:45:28-07:00","id":953112,"title":"","content":"I played a character with the Skill &quot;Soulforge&quot;. Wraith is fucked up. You torture a soul until it becomes a brick. You Break a person of everything. Tzim with vis wish they could do that.<br /> <br /> On a more Dark humor direction, I once played a Sabbat member who invented a game during a seige called &quot;Battleship&quot; we'd divide up the city and blow up various places if you hit like an Elysium or a haven you got points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:57:51-07:00","id":953138,"title":"","content":"Oh I see this thread being very productive......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:28:16-07:00","id":953315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/952975-whats-the-most-morally-ethically-fucked-up-things-your-pc-s-ever-done?p=953138#post953138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I see this thread being very productive......</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm hoping to grab a few ideas, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:23:43-07:00","id":953383,"title":"","content":"An idea from a VTT game I played on aol over a decade ago?<br /> <br /> My uketena ahroun just stood in stupefied Shock when her Alpha decided to let some Captured DNA scientists all go with a slap on the wrist... <br /> <br /> (scientist who HAD cruelly tortured captured garou) <br /> <br /> I was too busy being confounded to do anything about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:36:03-07:00","id":953795,"title":"","content":"Played a Mage inspired by Greek myth, drawing his power from there. He cursed a man so that he would only ejaculate spiders, scorpions and centipedes unless he ejaculated into his lawfully wedded wife (the victim was single).<br /> <br /> There's mythological precedence for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:54:42-07:00","id":953874,"title":"","content":"Had a player once who played a Mage with Mind 5, Prime 4, and Time 4 (Hermetic specializing in Mind). He was a good-ish sort, and would help trauma victims and what have you (basically go to people who had suffered greatly, and take the actual traumatic memories from the person, and &quot;suspend&quot; them into tass baubles made from energy harvested from some place or other in the High Umbra that deals with memory. So he collected these for a while, anytime he would save someone from something horrifying, or he'd just go to hospitals (the VA in particular), prisons, etc. And he just collected all this trauma and misery. Then he performed a ritual, the underlying metaphysics of which we negotiated and agreed upon, which allowed him to combine all that misery into a sort of compacted, fluid memory &quot;package&quot; for lack of a better word, and made multiple copies of this thing--at great expense and time, I should add. He went onto use these things as weapons--basically doing a memory dump into people using the Mind and Time (to make them &quot;live&quot; the memories quicky)--and it <i>wrecked</i> anyone he used it on. We ended up working out a system by which the person would make what amounts to a Willpower saving throw to mitigate the effects, but mostly they would end up in extreme shock or catatonic on the floor in the fetal position, or both, and develop at least one derangement (had a random table of appropriate derangements which favored post-traumatic stress), and would continue having to roll or get more derangements over a number of days dictated by that Willpower roll I mentioned. So basically a mind nuke (the rotes, ritual, and overall process for accomplishing this fear were eventually determined to be &quot;forbidden knowledge&quot; by the Order, as making someone live all those traumatic experiences is tantamount to having actually done all that awful stuff to them... which isn't cool. Also he took automatic Jhor resonance for basically eviscerating someone's psyche).<br /> <br /> The other thing that was pointed out by other players was that effectively robbing people of their traumatic memories was a &quot;good deed&quot; of dubious goodness. But mostly the effed up part was forcing any given person to live, in a few moments, the equivalent of dozens upon dozens (if not hundreds) of different trauma victims' most horrifying and terrible experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:52:07-07:00","id":953893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/952975-whats-the-most-morally-ethically-fucked-up-things-your-pc-s-ever-done?p=953874#post953874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why this practice was forbidden but a would put it hardly in the sphere of super-mega-evil-disturbing(TM), it's more of a ghost rider approach unless this guy used it on innocent bystanders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:59:55-07:00","id":953937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/952975-whats-the-most-morally-ethically-fucked-up-things-your-pc-s-ever-done?p=953893#post953893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see why this practice was forbidden but a would put it hardly in the sphere of super-mega-evil-disturbing(TM), it's more of a ghost rider approach unless this guy used it on innocent bystanders.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, what Ghost Rider does is force upon a perpetrator whatever painful experiences or anguish said perpetrator has inflicted upon others. It is the ultimately eye-for-an-eye, inasmuch as it's perfectly proportional: the person gets exactly whatever they gave.<br /> <br /> What made the practice in my game truly heinous is two-fold: first off, it's a one-size-fits-all attack; everybody gets slammed with the same pain/anguish cocktail--and while no one <i>per se</i> &quot;innocent&quot; was ever hit with the attack, given the means by which the player went about constructing this horror show, it simply cannot be said that any one person perpetrated all of the awful things that gave rise to the messed up memories that comprise the attack--that is to say that, unlike with Ghost Rider, getting hit with this thing is never even arguably 1:1 proportional to whatever awful thing they may have done to visit my player's wrath upon them.<br /> <br /> Second, there is arguably no difference between actually doing <i>something </i>to someone and forcing them to experience a perfect simulation of that <i>something</i>, such that the end effect psychologically is the same as if the <i>something </i>had in fact happened to them. In this instance, dropping this trauma bomb on people is the equivalent of perpetrating against them all the heinous individual acts that person will experience. Certainly (or <i>hopefully</i>) we would agree that it is never acceptable (from a normative humanitarian/human rights perspective) to torture people, use sexual assault as a weapon, burn people alive, or anything else of the sort--and yet, here was my player, a nominal &quot;good guy&quot; who was <i>essentially</i> inflicting hours and hours of all those things and worse on enemies in the blink of an eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:47:00-07:00","id":954009,"title":"","content":"Once again, I am reminded why I think that all Mages are psychopaths in training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:21:36-07:00","id":955928,"title":"","content":"Most of my WoD characters have tended to be somewhat benevolent or at least honorable, so even for the former Sabbat one excesses tended to be in the realm of ruthlessness shown to sworn enemies rather than general malevolence. Though my very first was a frightening child vampire modeled on Felicity Latimer from Bill Garnet's <i>Down-Bound Train\u2014</i>I once had her avenge humiliating disrespect from another character by stalking all his friends, embracing them, and surprising him with their diablerized corpses arrayed into a tableau in his office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:48:44-07:00","id":955938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/952975-whats-the-most-morally-ethically-fucked-up-things-your-pc-s-ever-done?p=954009#post954009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, I am reminded why I think that all Mages are psychopaths in training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less psychopaths and more Blue and Orange Morality.<br /> <br /> That said, from a practical standpoint, the difference is really academic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}